\tag{fdip}
\title{Continuum approximation and geometric realization}
\date{2026-10-31}

\p{A finite operator can approximate a supplied continuum space, or its
carrier can be assigned a geometric realization. These are different
questions: approximation needs comparison maps and a limit, while
realization needs a specified construction and a choice of information
to preserve. The [circle calculation](fdip-004G) answers a small
approximation question using pairings, positive precision and Gaussian
moments. The realization question is left for the subsequent comparison.}

\transclude{fdip-004G}
